			"notes": "# Irminsul 20260724-0001 Beta\n\nThis is a beta/test build. Use it on a test server, mirrored world, or staged rollout first. Keep world and Ledger data backups before testing rollback, purge, or high-volume logging.\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- Minecraft: 1.21.11\n- Java: 21\n- Fabric Loader: 0.18.5 or newer\n- Fabric API: 0.141.4+1.21.11 or newer\n- Fabric Language Kotlin: 1.13.12+kotlin.2.4.0 or newer\n\n## Highlights\n\n- Reworked Irminsul storage, cold-segment summaries, counting, and query planning to reduce scans during broad and long-range searches.\n- Added batched page reads and page-window prefetching so navigation avoids repeated counts and redundant database work.\n- Preserved offline player aliases and UUID lookups, including migration support for existing SQL databases.\n- Added bounded, fixed-lifetime result caching with stale-query protection and targeted fetching of only missing client pages.\n- Expanded regression coverage for storage codecs, recovery, pagination, command parsing, offline players, and cache behavior.\n\n## Usage\n\n- Enable the backend with `engine = \"irminsul\"` in `config/ledger.toml`.\n- The default data directory is `world/ledger-irminsul`.\n- This release is still experimental and is not recommended for an important production server without tested backups and a rollback plan.\n\n**Full changelog:** https://github.com/BorderRegion/Irminsul/compare/irminsul-20260615-0001...irminsul-20260724-0001"
		},
