			"notes": "# Irminsul irminsul-20260615-0001 Beta\n\nThis is a beta/test build. Use it on a test server, mirrored world, or staged rollout first. Keep world and Ledger data backups before testing rollback or high-volume logging.\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- Minecraft: 1.21.11\n- Fabric Loader: 0.18.5 or newer\n- Fabric API: 0.141.4+1.21.11 or newer\n- Fabric Language Kotlin: 1.13.12+kotlin.2.4.0 or newer\n\n## Notes\n\n- Irminsul is an experimental Ledger fork with a local append-only backend.\n- Enable the backend with `engine = \"irminsul\"` in `config/ledger.toml`.\n- The default Irminsul data directory is `world/ledger-irminsul`.\n- This release stabilizes rollback/restore/purge orchestration, queue spill recovery, command/network error handling, and Irminsul startup recovery checks.\n- Rollback, restore, and purge now drain queued writes before operating and block follow-up operations after a failed rollback-state persistence marker.\n- The current benchmark dataset showed 20588 actions, about 1.50 MB of Irminsul data, and about 5x-16x faster current-path search/rollback candidate queries than the existing Ledger MySQL query path.\n- Hand-tuned MySQL queries can close part of the gap, so the benchmark is a comparison against Ledger's current SQL/JDBC query shape rather than a general limit of MySQL.\n- This release is not recommended for an important production server without tested backups and a rollback plan."
		},
